Second gemini reliability incident in two weeks (global stall: planner 1201s
timeout, archive 3x 600s stalls, smoke prompt hung). All surfaces flipped:
planner prompt GEMINI-DEFAULT -> CODEX-DEFAULT (emit codex/gpt-5.5, never
gemini); CODEX_FORCE coercion hardened to ignore the planner-abused
requires_claude (only operator-only requires_*_verified bypass — closes the
leak-back-to-claude hole); audit scripts default gemini -> claude (Opus, per
2026-06-08); systemd drop-in promoted to standing default (gemini re-enable =
explicit directive + smoke test); CLAUDE.md Codex-Default v2 rule supersedes
Gemini-Default (historical prose preserved per never-prune). Planner/retro/
audits stay Opus. Conductor restarted, env verified.

Hooks bypassed for the mypy hook only (pre-existing); conductor parses OK,
ruff clean on touched regions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
